Ubuntu 24.04 (x86-64): install the release .deb, then start the server with melodica-pianod2 -c /usr/share/melodica-pianod2/html. The packaged control client is /usr/share/melodica-pianod2/piano.

pianod2 for Melodica

Build release 421 with Pandora support using the original configure and make instructions below. Its Pandora media source uses the Melodica tuner codec. Set MELODICA_SCROBBLE_TOKEN for the account running the server to your personal client token from https://spacegho.st/scrobble/account/. All listeners sharing that server then contribute its Pandora playback to that account. Remove the variable and restart to disconnect. Local files and station inserts are excluded.

pianod
======
pianod is a daemon style music player that supports multiple sources.

- mix from multiple sources
- interface it as a music player backend to home automation systems
- multiple outputs, each with their own users and audio ("rooms")
- script playlist changes and mixing via at(1), nc(1) and/or shell scripts
- automatic playlist selection (autotuning) based on music preferences of
  those connected/present/listening.
- Includes a web-based client served with the integrated web server.
- Or write your own using line-oriented or websocket protocols.

The project home page is: http://deviousfish.com/pianod

See AUTHORS for a list of authors and contributors.
See COPYING for license information.
See INSTALL for installation instructions.
